# D10(a) NEGATIVE (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06): a local `&`-bind must
# not dodge the rejection by hiding in a `do:` block whose TAIL is a
# STATEMENT-FORM match whose arm yields a borrow. This shape dodged the
# expr-only recursion and garbage-linked (undefined reference to
# `int64_t__push`) before `block_tail_is_borrow_bind` recursed statement-form
# `match` arm bodies / else. ⚠ The match arms must be INDENTED MULTI-LINE
# bodies — an inline `case X: <body>` in a do-tail stmt-match is a parse error
# regardless of `&`.
# Expected: error[E_LocalBorrowBind] at the initializer.
void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] b = [4, 5]
    int n = 1
    auto r = do:
        match n:
            case 1:
                &a
            else:
                &b
    r.push(9)
    print(r.len())
